# --- Secrets / env ---
# `**/.env` is belt-and-braces: rag-service/.env holds a Supabase *service-role*
# key, which bypasses row-level security entirely. rag-service/.gitignore covers
# it too, and one of the two failing open is not a risk worth carrying.
/.env
**/.env
# Any decorated variant too — `.env.bak`, `.env.old`, `.env.local`. Splitting the
# service key out of the root file produces backups, and `**/.env` alone does not
# cover them, so a copy of a service-role key would sit stageable in the tree.
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# --- Dependencies ---
/node_modules

# --- Next.js build output ---
/.next
/out
next-env.d.ts

# --- Test / coverage ---
/coverage

# --- Python (rag-service) ---
.venv/
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Logs ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Deploy ---
.vercel

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Build / tooling scratch ---
/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache

# --- Tooling / agent scratch (working-tree only) ---
/.claude
/.superpowers
/.gstack
/docs/superpowers
# The session progress file. Same species as the specs and plans above: it is a
# running note between sessions, not a repo artifact, and it churns on every
# session in a way that adds noise to every diff. It stays in the working tree —
# untracked means it is yours alone, and a fresh clone will not have it.
/HANDOFF.md
.gstack/
